REPRO (perl 5.40.3):
  my $f = '/etc/hostname';
  open(FILE, " $f") or die "open1 failed: $!";   print "1 ok\n";
  open(my $fh, "< $f  ") or die "open2 failed: $!"; print "2 ok\n";
  open(F3, "  <$f") or die "open3 failed: $!";    print "3 ok\n";
perl: 1 ok / 2 ok / 3 ok.  PCL: dies "open1 failed: No such file or directory".

perlfunc open (2-arg): leading and trailing white space is stripped from the filename (the reason the 3-arg form exists).  Layer: the runtime's 2-arg open mode parser (cl/pcl-runtime.lisp, p-open's string-spec split).  Acceptance: YAML-Tiny 12_write.t rows 2-4 (blessed to this task by s531a) -- one-file run `tools/run-dist-t.pl --rows cpan-tests/modules/YAML-Tiny-1.74 t/12_write.t` 1/3 -> 4/0.  Probe: s531a scratch/s531a/pr/open2ws.pl.

